%I A400824 #16 Nov 10 2026 13:18:59
%S A400824 0,0,0,6,46,314,2224,16414,124542,960626,7478688,58522422
%N A400824 Number of Type A palindromes of generation 1 (pairs of major star triples, PA(1)) in the level-n supertile of the Spectre tiling.
%C A400824 The level-n supertile is obtained from a single Spectre tile by n inflation steps of the S8/S9 substitution and contains A057080(n) tiles. A star triple is a set of three Spectre tiles related by a rotation through 120 degrees about a common point of their boundaries.
%C A400824 Star triples arise on the seams of the inflation steps and form clusters there. The clusters are chains of three kinds of megaobjects: Type A megastars (A397120), Type C megastars (A400810) and Type A palindromes (A400811).
%C A400824 The Type A palindrome of generation g, PA(g), has A400811(g) = 2*(A397120(1) + ... + A397120(g)) star triples. It is a chain of Type A megastars MA(g), ..., MA(2), MA(1), MA(1), MA(2), ..., MA(g); its two halves are related by a rotation through 180 degrees about the center, which is PA(1), a pair of major star triples, that is, two copies of MA(1). PA(g) is created at level g+2 and afterwards only copied.
%C A400824 Therefore the same sequence counts the copies of every generation: the level-n supertile contains a(n) copies of PA(1), a(n-1) copies of PA(2), a(n-2) copies of PA(3), and in general a(n-g+1) copies of PA(g), for 1 <= g <= n-2. Every Type A palindrome appears in 6 copies at the level where it is created, in 46 copies one level later, in 314 two levels later, and so on.
%C A400824 The number of star triples in all Type A palindromes of the level-n supertile is A400822(n) = Sum_{g=1..n-2} A400811(g)*a(n-g+1).
%C A400824 a(0)-a(7) were obtained by direct counts in the level-n supertiles. The other terms and the formulas follow from the growth rules of the clusters and megaobjects; they are not proved.
%H A400824 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="/A400824/b400824.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..100</a>
