%H A400824 David Smith, Joseph Samuel Myers, Craig S. Kaplan, and Chaim Goodman-Strauss, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17743">A chiral aperiodic monotile</a>, arXiv:2305.17743 [math.CO], 2023-2024.
%F A400824 Conjecture: a(n) = 13*a(n-1) - 44*a(n-2) + 28*a(n-3) + 5*a(n-4) - a(n-5) for n >= 7.
%F A400824 Conjectured g.f.: 2*x^3*(3 - 16*x - 10*x^2 - x^3)/((1 - x)*(1 - 8*x + x^2)*(1 - 4*x - x^2)).
%F A400824 Conjecture: a(n) = 4*A001090(n-2) - A001090(n-3) + A014445(n-1)/2 - 2 for n >= 3.
%F A400824 Limit_{n->oo} a(n)/A057080(n) = (275*sqrt(15) - 1065)/10 = 0.0070420207... (one PA(1) for every (275*sqrt(15) + 1065)/15 = 142.0046946... tiles).
%F A400824 Conjecture: the number of Type A palindromes of all generations in the level-n supertile is Sum_{m=3..n} a(m) = (A001090(n-1) + A001090(n-2))/2 + A015448(n)/4 - 2*n + 9/4 for n >= 3 (6, 52, 366, 2590, ...); its limit ratio to A057080(n) is (5 - sqrt(15))/(2*(35 + 9*sqrt(15))) = 0.0080659... (one Type A palindrome for every 62 + 16*sqrt(15) = 123.968... tiles).
%e A400824 a(3) = 6: the level-3 supertile (559 tiles) contains 18 major star triples (A400813(3)); 12 of them form 6 Type A palindromes of generation 1, and the other 6 are Type A megastars of generation 1.
%e A400824 a(4) = 4*8 - 1 + 34/2 - 2 = 46.
%e A400824 The level-5 supertile contains a(5) = 314 copies of PA(1), a(4) = 46 copies of PA(2) and a(3) = 6 copies of PA(3), together 366 Type A palindromes with 314*2 + 46*10 + 6*60 = 1448 = A400822(5) star triples.
%t A400824 CoefficientList[Series[2 x^3 (3 - 16 x - 10 x^2 - x^3)/((1 - x) (1 - 8 x + x^2) (1 - 4 x - x^2)), {x, 0, 23}], x]
